+# Native parametric stamping family
+
+`pattern_transform` is fixed for the whole episode.
+
+- `as_drawn` preserves the exact canonical program: extract the yellow offsets
+  inside the blue frame and stamp them at every orange seed.
+- `quarter_turn` first extracts the same input-dependent exemplar, then rotates
+  those offsets clockwise and stamps the rotated pattern at every seed.
+
+The shared input grammar admits one complete blue frame, one connected yellow
+exemplar anchored at the interior top-left and spanning the interior, and one to
+four nonoverlapping orange seed placements that fit under both settings.  Inputs
+are sampled independently of the private setting.  The adapter supports 2--6
+stable-prefix demonstrations and 1--4 stable-prefix queries; the fourth query is
+a substantive 30x30 boundary case.
+
+Sequential dependency: step A locates the frame and produces the exemplar offset
+set plus frame interior height.  Step B consumes those values to choose either
+the original offsets or the clockwise-quarter-turn offsets before painting every
+seed footprint.  The retained protected-Racket witness substitutes the unrotated
+intermediate in a qualified `quarter_turn` episode and changes the final output.
+
+`audit.py` checks bounded seed/count coverage, finite declared rivals, input
+uniqueness, and Python-claim consistency.  It is local authoring evidence, not
+owner acceptance or universal identifiability.
